        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1137">

                <pb facs="0852" n="776" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg776"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/238</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spanish Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 21, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Spanish Chargé d’Affaires in Mexico,
                    Sr. Cárdenas, telegraphs me under date of yesterday, that he is endeavoring to
                    obtain from the Government of General Carranza the repeal of a <pb facs="0853"
                        n="777" xml:id="pg777"/> decree which is causing great prejudice to the
                    Spanish cotton growers and to the cotton textile industry in Mexico.</p>
                <p>This decree obliges owner of cotton to sell their produce to a commission
                    appointed by the Government, and at a price fixed by the commission, and Sr.
                    Cárdenas is trying to obtain from the authorities in the capital, if not a
                    repeal of the decree in question, at least that the contracts made by the cotton
                    growers previously to the publication of the decree may be respected.</p>
                <p>I should consider it a great favor if you could instruct the American
                    representative at the capital to give Sr. Cárdenas his assistance in the
                    protection of these interests.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Riaño</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
